# Guardian project-level npm configuration.
#
# Redirects the npm download cache OUT of the repository directory into /tmp.
# Rationale: in sandboxed development environments (Arena/Replit-style) the
# workspace directory is snapshot-persisted; npm's default cache (~/.npm)
# then accumulates thousands of files inside the persisted workspace and can
# exceed persistence budgets. /tmp is never persisted, so the cache is
# naturally ephemeral.
#
# This is intentional, non-destructive, and safe to delete if you prefer the
# npm default cache location on your machine.
cache=/tmp/guardian-npm-cache
